                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is a healthy return rate for a fashion D2C brand?</h3>
                                        <p>For womenswear: 20-28% is healthy. For menswear: 12-20%. For accessories / footwear: 8-15%. Above 30% on womenswear needs an intervention (size chart, fit tech, or product-line fix).</p>
                                        <h3>Should a fashion brand launch in India first or Dubai first?</h3>
                                        <p>Depends on category. Ethnic / fusion: India-first, then UAE for the diaspora market. Modest fashion: UAE-first, then India. Streetwear / athleisure: India offers volume; UAE offers margin. Most successful brands do both within 18 months.</p>
                                        <h3>Is Shopify Plus enough for fashion D2C at scale?</h3>
                                        <p>For most brands up to ~₹100 Cr ARR, yes. Above that, headless architectures start paying off for personalization, custom checkout, and complex omnichannel.</p>
                                        <h3>How much should I budget for size-fit tech?</h3>
                                        <p>$8K-40K/year for a SaaS tool like True Fit or Fit Analytics. $20K-100K one-time for AI body-scan integrations like 3DLOOK. ROI usually pays back in 4-9 months via return-rate reduction.</p>
